    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Delphi was a small city-state in Phocis that existed to run the sanctuary of Apollo and the most famous oracle of the Greek world.</li><li>The Amphictyonic League of twelve peoples protected the shrine, ran the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#pythian-games">Pythian Games</a> and could proclaim sacred wars.</li><li>Phocians, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#macedonian-empire">Macedonians</a>, Aetolians and finally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#roman-empire">Romans</a> controlled it in turn, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#greece">Greece</a> came under Roman oversight in 146 BCE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#greeks">Greeks</a> believed Delphi was the centre of the earth: Zeus released two eagles from opposite ends of the world and they met there, a spot marked by a stone navel, the omphalos.</p></aside>
    </section>

